All issues are fixed, verified, and pushed in commit `770962f` (39 files). The dev server is now live in your Preview tab at `http://localhost:60973`.

**What was fixed**

- **Landing navbar overflow at 768px** — the desktop nav was displayed while the hamburger was hidden, squeezing “Sign In” into two lines and clipping the CTA. The full nav now appears at `lg`, the mobile menu covers tablet widths, the CTA shortens on small screens, and all actions are `shrink-0`/`whitespace-nowrap`. The navbar also no longer nests an `<a>` inside another `<a>`. See [landing-navbar.tsx](features/landing/landing-navbar.tsx).
- **Timezone pill and popover** — the trigger no longer wraps at 1024px, and the popover clamps its height to the viewport so it stays usable on short screens. See [timezone-selector.tsx](components/timezone-selector.tsx).
- **Anime details stuck on “Loading anime”** — the inline theme script sat inside the React body tree and broke React’s streamed Suspense reveal, so details content stayed hidden. Theme bootstrapping now loads from [theme-init.js](public/theme-init.js) as a pre-paint script; content reveals normally and light/dark selection persists across reloads.
- **Hydration mismatches** — relative airing labels now tick from a server-provided timestamp via [use-now.ts](lib/use-now.ts) instead of reading `Date.now()` during render.
- **Error handling** — route-level boundaries for the app shell, the top-level app, and a last-resort global error screen.
- **Security/SEO** — nosniff, frame denial, referrer and permissions policies, HSTS in production, plus `robots.txt` and `sitemap.xml` routes.
- **Privacy copy** — removed “encrypted” claims; copy now accurately describes account-scoped data protected by row-level security.
- **Per-request performance** — `getViewer()` is memoized per request, and the schedule page loads only library entries instead of hydrating full library metadata.
- **Lint** — cleaned all 32 unused-import/variable warnings; ESLint is now completely clean.
- **QA script** — corrected stale expectations for the landing page shell and the details page’s franchise section. See [qa-responsive.mjs](scripts/qa-responsive.mjs).

**Verification run**

- `npm run typecheck` — passed
- `npx eslint .` — 0 errors, 0 warnings
- `npx vitest run` — 215 tests across 18 files passed
- `npm run build` — passed
- Responsive QA at 320/390/768/1024/1440px — all 25 page checks and 5 flows passed with 0px overflow, including light theme
- Confirmed the details page renders its real content (no loading lock), relations section present, theme applies after reload, and no hydration/anchor warnings remain

One limitation: I verified the theme script runs and persists, but did not measure the first-paint flash frame-by-frame.

If you want to lock these fixes against regressions, the details-page streaming bug deserves an end-to-end test.
